        "original_id": "df891422-5218-5c62-a46a-7711476cd0b4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Langley Regional Airport, Langley, British Columbia, Canada\n- Organizations: Canadian Museum of Flight, Canadian Museum of Flight Association\n- Products: Helicopters, fixed-wing aircraft, VTOL aircraft\n- Systems: helipads\n- Topics: helicopter operations, aviation museums\n\nFacts:\n- Langley Regional Airport has three helipads, and helicopter operations are a major part of the airport's traffic.\n- Helicopters can be used in congested or isolated areas where fixed-wing aircraft and many VTOL aircraft cannot operate.\n- Since 1998, the Canadian Museum of Flight has formally been the Canadian Museum of Flight Association.\n- The Canadian Museum of Flight is an aviation museum located at Langley Regional Airport in Langley, British Columbia, Canada.",
